[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Today I\'m testing Reineo\'s newest smart glasses, the Reneo IO. The lightest glasses ever released by them at 33 gram, 449 bucks, brand new. And we\'re going to find out if they\'re worth the'

[00:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'investment in this video. But first, Riley Peterson 5997. You just won giveaway number one, the Meta Adventurer glasses. So, make sure to check your email so I can get those sent over immediately. And we\'re actually doing'

[00:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even more glasses giveaways very soon, new ones. And you can\'t win if you\'re not subscribed. So, make sure you subscribe right now and fill out that giveaway form in the description. I know you guys thought it was over. It\'s just'

[00:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'beginning. Now, Raino did send me these so I could test and review them before release, but I can say whatever I want to about them, good or bad, and that\'s exactly what I plan to do. When you open the box, the first thing you\'ll find is'

[00:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the standard non-charging case for the glasses, but there\'s actually quite a bit of other things included, too. You get extra silicone ear covers if you want a little more comfort around the temples, an extra large set of adjustable nose pads in case the'

[01:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'standard ones aren\'t big enough for you. A Reo cleaning cloth to clean the lenses. Extra screws and even a matching screwdriver. Then there\'s this USBC charging adapter that attaches directly'

[01:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to the front of the glasses, which is how you can charge them if you don\'t have the optional charging case. And you might be wondering, where is this charging case? Well, you can optionally get that included for an extra 50 bucks as part of their $499 bundle, which'

[01:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually comes in this separate box. Now, the charging case has a design that\'s more unique than you might think because when you look closer, the bottom portion is actually translucent. I didn\'t notice this at first, but you can'

[01:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually see the glasses through the case partially, which I think just makes this case look super super cool. And then we have the Raino IO smart glasses. And my first reaction was these look really slim and they\'re insanely'

[01:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lightweight. For comparison, the Rayben Meta non-dis glasses, the most popular smart glasses in the world with no display, are 49 g, 16 g or 50% heavier than these, which have dual displays. On'

[02:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'top of that, it also has 50/50 weight distribution, which essentially means it\'s equally weighted front to back. So, it\'s not going to feel like it\'s tugging on the back of your ears, falling downward, and it\'s also not going to feel that way in the front. So,'

[02:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'combining that with how ultra ultra lightweight these are, and these are just really comfortable, and they look really nice and feel like normal glasses, which is really cool. But like for Reineo, who previously had made the Reineo X3 Pro X2, these are by far the'

[02:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'best looking, lightest, and easily the closest to normal glasses in appearance that they have ever made. And the material also took a great direction in my opinion. They\'re built with magnesium'

[02:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'aluminum with titanium temples. So basically the entire build feels like very metallic. Feels really premium which is way way better than the shiny or even matte plastic that all of the'

[02:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Ray-B band metas and Meta Glasses have been using. It feels better to the touch. It\'s more smudge proof. It feels cooler on your face, less sticky, and they just feel more high quality. And they\'re also IP54 dust resistant and water resistant, which is great. And'

[03:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'look at this. For controls, we have probably my favorite hardware feature. this little knob on the top which they call the smart crown. So basically you can rotate this forward and backward. It\'s very tactile. Has like little grips'

[03:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on the side and you can press it or double press it or tap and hold it for different functions. It gives you a lot of different ways to control them without having to swipe side to side on the side of your glasses with traditional touchpad. So my opinion this'

[03:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'is a great innovation. I actually like this a lot better than doing this. Basically you\'re going to rotate forward and backward to navigate through the menu is a custom heads-up display. Pressing it will enter into like sort of the app selection or select whatever'

[03:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you\'re hovering over. Double tapping at any moment is a custom setting. So by default, this will be the AI that will come up and you can ask it whatever questions you want. But you can set it to other things too, like the various apps that they have in these glasses.'

[03:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And then if you press and hold, it\'s going to go back to the home screen. That can be customized too, by the way, when it\'s off. So you\'re getting two customizable controls through like the button presses there. Now, one really important thing that you should know about these glasses before we go any'

[04:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'further is that they don\'t have speakers. It\'s part of the reason they\'re extremely lightweight. I can\'t believe how light these are. It\'s crazy. But yeah, if you want speakers, these don\'t have them. And if you need a camera on the front, these don\'t have'

[04:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that either. So, if you need speakers and camera, just click off this video, stop watching. But if you\'re still interested in these glasses, want to see all the cool apps that they still have in them and just how crazy they kind of are, you might want to keep watching. But, um, just because they don\'t have'

[04:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'speakers doesn\'t mean they don\'t have microphones. So they actually have a four microphone array system that\'s able to detect if the speaker is talking from in front of you if you\'re the one speaking and also get group conversations going on around you if you happen to be talking with a bunch of'

[04:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'people and obviously pick up for captions translation AI questions all that stuff meetings and to help with the voice isolation they actually have a bone conduction sensor which is cool right now especially in the current climate the no camera thing is kind of'

[04:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'really nice because you\'re not having to deal with all that weird backlash that smart glasses are having because of meta all the privacy stuff. These are just going to look like normal glasses. These feel the most like normal glasses I\'ve ever worn out of smart glasses. However, even though these don\'t have speakers or'

[05:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'camera, there\'s still a surprising amount these glasses can do and they\'ve been kind of taking from the best competition around to make a really cool inclusive product and adding a bunch of their own little features to it. So,'

[05:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'let\'s get into that. So, first off, you have a display in both eyes using microLEDs and waveguides with a 23.5 degree field of view up to,300 nits of brightness and a green monochrome display. So, bigger FOV than the Meta'

[05:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Rayban displays at 20, but not quite as big as InMogo 3 for reference. Now, by far my favorite thing about Reo IO\'s display, particularly is they\'ve chosen to make the immediate screen upon waking them up actually useful instead of just'

[05:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'being a screen full of apps to select from when you turn them on. So, like Memomind, like EVG2s, you\'re getting a fully customizable HUD style dashboard with multiple screens. And it\'s just'

[06:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'such a no-brainer for smart glasses companies these days. I don\'t know why more companies and brands aren\'t doing it because full screen of apps when you turn on the glasses is not that like inherently they\'re useless until you go'

[06:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'into one of those apps. With these, you turn on the screen by the way, which you can either do by tapping the button or just looking up. It\'s like the moment. It\'s great. I love it. And then you just do that. You have all the information that you custom set, the widgets that'

[06:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you custom set to see first. And then you can just like move on about your day if you want. You don\'t even have to use any of the other cool features of the glasses. It\'s just a really useful way to have them not just be like a smartphone on your face where you have'

[06:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to navigate menus to actually get to useful information. It\'s all right there right away and I love that. So, let\'s talk about that custom heads-up display. You can have up to three different screens with different widgets that you select and info available just by'

[06:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'looking up and navigating between them with the little dial here. As of right now on this heads-up display, you\'re always going to see the time, date, day of week, battery level, weather, and temperature. But in addition to that, the extra widgets you can choose are'

[07:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to-dos, which you can check off individually within the glasses. You don\'t have to go in the app or anything. You can have a full weather breakdown for your city by the hour for 5 hours with the temperature and actual weather'

[07:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'conditions. You can connect your email to this, which I\'ve connected my Gmail. So, it\'s going to show the most recent email, a little preview of it, what sort of the content and first words are, and then it\'s going to show how many emails you actually have unread, which is now'

[07:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'look at my number. There you can connect your calendar too which is great. Another widget you can use. You\'re also getting stocks and even a world clock if you want to always know what time it is in a certain other part of the world'

[07:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which is really useful. You\'re also getting notifications that pop up on your display on your glasses in your field of view. Notifications which from your phone I might add. So this could be text messages, emails, app notifications. And you can actually'

[07:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'filter out specifically which apps you want to send notifications to the glasses and which ones you don\'t. So you can have it be very focused if you want. So those are sort of the more basic has a display type features. Now let\'s get into the more advanced ones. The first of which is AI. So by default if you'

[08:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'double tap the crown button the AI is going to pop up. You\'re going to be able to read like what do you want to ask? And then you can say whatever you want. How\'s it going? I was wondering if there\'s any events'

[08:22] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'today. When\'s the best time to go to the beach today? Now, if you actually press the smart'

[08:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'crown, you\'ll get access to basically select from their more advanced apps. So, here you can scroll left and right on the wheel to look at the different options. The first of which is going to be live caption. So, if you press the smart crown again to select this, it\'s'

[08:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'going to default to the languages you selected in their phone app. So, by default, I have it on English to English, but if you go into the radio app, you can actually change this. So, it\'ll effectively become live translation instead. And it\'s going to have 109 different accents and 55'

[09:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different languages, which is crazy. Super super cool. And you can set the caption/transation to default between face-toface interactions or group interactions. So, it\'s either going to'

[09:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'listen just to the person in front of you or it\'s going to listen to like everyone in the room besides you. I actually prefer the group listening mode after trying both because unless you\'re in a really loud setting, the group mode is still get the person in front of you anyways. So, unless you\'re trying to'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cancel out more voices, then you\'re probably going to want it on the group mode because it\'s going to hear the most that way. It\'s also worth noting that the captions, the translation, it just shows you what they\'re saying, translates what they\'re saying, puts it in front of your view. It\'s not going to like repeat the own words that you just'

[09:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'said into here. So, that is something worth noting. So, right here, it\'s just showing the English words, like, "Hello, I want cookies." I actually said all this in Spanish with the glasses being held in front of me and sort of facing me like this because again, it detects'

[09:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the person talking to them, not the person wearing them when it does the translation/captions. Now, I did pretty well, bearing in mind that my Spanish sucks, but it still got it. And specifically, I was really impressed by just the number of Spanish options they'

[10:10] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had. There\'s 20 different like countries that speak Spanish, and you get their individual Spanish accents there. It even has a different one for US Spanish versus Spanish and Mexico. So, there\'s so much distinction and individual'

[10:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'nuance you can get there. It\'s just really cool for live translation. The next app in these is going to be the teleprompter. Now, lots of display glasses are incorporating teleprompterss by default now. So, do these actually bother to set themselves apart or are'

[10:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'they just the same as all the other ones? So, luckily the first thing I noticed when playing with this is that there\'s actually a decent amount of customization that you don\'t normally see with teleprompterss and smart glasses. So, first off, there\'s three'

[10:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'different modes. There\'s presentation mode, where it tries to fit sort of more words on the screen and puts the screen higher up. Then there\'s video creation mode, which puts the words lower down, so they\'re more centered in your field of view, so it doesn\'t look like you\'re looking above someone the whole time.'

[11:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'And then you have custom mode, which is the third. Next is the settings for actually scrolling through the teleprompter. So, there\'s three different settings for that, too. You have AI smart follow, which I\'m using right now, which detects the words you\'re saying and automatically scrolls'

[11:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for you. And by the way, I\'m getting five lines, about 10 words on each line, so like 50 words on the screen at once. And it\'s really good at following the exact word I\'m on. Then there\'s autoscroll mode where you can just'

[11:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'select a specific speed that you want it to scroll through. And it\'s going to be constant when scrolling, so you can keep a certain pace, maybe finish your speech by a certain time. And then there\'s manual mode where you can actually control the exact moments you want it to'

[11:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scroll with the smart crown on the side of that. Cool thing about this is you can have it on the AI autoscroll mode and if you accidentally go on a tangent or it happens to not catch something you said, which doesn\'t happen too often,'

[11:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but you can still do the manual scroll while doing the AI autoscroll. Really, really useful. Really, really versatile. Doesn\'t lock you into one mode. Yeah, you can combine manual scrolling with the AI autoscroll, which will automatically resume when you take your'

[12:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hand off of this and stop scrolling. On top of that, when you\'re in this teleprompter mode, I can see the time that I\'ve been talking in the bottom left with a clock icon, and I can see the percentage of the way through the script that I wrote that I am, which right now is 61%. The other really nice'

[12:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'thing about the teleprompter in these is once you have the scripts sort of pasted into the app, titled different things, you can actually like go through into the teleprompter app and select the exact like speech or whatever that you want to give and like swipe through'

[12:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'them. You don\'t have to have your phone out to do any of it. It\'s really cool. And the crazy thing is like the most archaic teleprompter I\'ve used is in the meta displays which are $800. Like you have to open it and then like paste it in. I don\'t even think you can have'

[12:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'multiple documents on it and then it\'s not autoscroll at all to manually scroll through everything and then they\'re one display. So your eye burning by the end of your speech. See that\'s the difference right? That\'s like bare minimum teleprompter on on the meta displays. They just like threw it in'

[12:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'there so they could say it as a feature. And with these they added as many features as they could. Made it customizable. made is you could use multiple different modes in one and you can scroll through, choose all of them in the glasses without needing to like do it on your phone. They add all these things and it\'s not going to add to'

[13:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'their marketing. They\'re just doing it because it makes the feature better. And I don\'t know why more companies don\'t do that. It\'s kind of annoying that like Meta has all these resources and then sometimes when they\'re building out specific like literal features for their glasses, they just get to the minimum'

[13:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'level and then just leave it there so they can call it a feature. So far, you\'ll see more in this video, but the Rainos don\'t do that. They try to take the features that everyone else has and actually make things that are better about them and make them function better than the other brands. Anyways, back to'

[13:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'what I was saying. The next app we\'re going to talk about is Voice Memo. This is another thing. It\'s just like a meeting summary, but they\'ve added extra features that make it different from other glasses that have audio recording and meeting summaries. At its base, it\'s'

[13:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just going to record a conversation when you tell it to start recording. going to transcribe the whole thing with the different speaker names and then it\'s going to provide an AI summary and different like bullet points information on this whole conversation meeting sounds pretty standard but they\'ve'

[13:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'actually done a few things to set them apart here like I mentioned first off if you single press the crown any point during your like voice recording it\'s going to flag at that timestamp so whatever is being talked about at that moment when you press the button it\'s going to pay special attention to that'

[14:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so during the AI summary it\'s going to like add extra focus to that part rather than just like sort of generalizing most of it and trying to find all the points specifically it\'s going to know that point is something that you found important and it\'s really easy to just'

[14:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'do that and bookmark it basically during the actual meeting or conversation. The next really cool thing they\'ve added is in your phone you can actually add notes. So like during meeting conversation whatever it is you can write a note while everyone is talking while you\'re talking and then it will'

[14:37] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'associate that note with that direct time stamp too. So the next feature is to-dos. I already kind of mentioned this, but basically you can go in into the to-dos app and then manually scroll through and select specific ones that you want to complete, like you\'re in a'

[14:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'video game. It\'s pretty cool. And then obviously when you go back, it\'ll refresh the main screen so that your new to-dos are on there and the ones you checked off are no longer on the list. Next is focus mode, which is basically just going to mute like your notifications, make the glasses not like do anything that\'s annoying to you.'

[15:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Finally, we have what might be the most interesting of all the features of these glasses, and that is what they\'re calling lifelog memory, which is in beta right now, and I will be testing it more over time, but so far, it\'s essentially'

[15:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'giving your glasses a form of ambient memory. So, throughout your day, like conversations will be had, things will be said, you\'ll ask the glasses certain things, log certain things, and it\'s going to help you organize it. It\'s going to come up with daily summaries,'

[15:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'which is really nice. Another great thing I loved in the Millions also present here being able to go through and ask things about your day that just happened and maybe you don\'t fully remember. It\'s really cool. I\'d love this to be added on more smart glasses.'

[15:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'It\'s a really really cool feature and it\'s nice that these have it too. And I\'m also excited to see the ways that Ray Neo is going to innovate on that and maybe add other new features to make it stand out more from the competition too. I I think it\'s going to be really cool. Like the fact that this is in beta, it\'s'

[15:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'already working with the daily summaries. I\'m pretty excited for this. The next big thing I want to talk about is the battery life. So, these have a 240 mAh battery. These are ridiculously tiny. That\'s a lot of battery fitting here. Even though these are so small,'

[16:03] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and that battery life is actually going to give you 2 days of use. Plus, this charging case, like these probably aren\'t going to die on you in like a week. Realistically, I\'ve had them for about that amount of time, and they haven\'t died. These glasses are'

[16:16] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'essentially going to just feel like they last forever, which is really, really, really cool. 2 days of battery life, and then this really good, nice charging case. They\'re just going to keep going. It\'s great. So, after testing all of these features, what do I think? I think'

[16:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the Reineal IO is actually more than meets the eye. They\'re $449 with the standard case or $4.99 with the charging case, which has this really cool translucent front to it, which I'

[16:42] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just love that you can like see through it. Like, look, you can see my finger. See, it\'s it\'s translucent. And honestly, that\'s a pretty decent package for this price, especially when you compare it to something like the Even G2s, which also don\'t have speakers,'

[16:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'have a lot of the same features as these, but they\'re $599 plus more than that if you get the Ring. But if there is one core feature I\'d say is missing from these, which I know they can do because they have it in the Raino'

[17:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'X3 Pro, that\'s going to be mass navigation. I\'m just saying this because it works so well in the Raino X3 Pro, like the integrated compass and everything. It\'s like impossible to get lost with those. So, if they could integrate that like map system or some'

[17:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'version of it into these glasses, I think that would just be like the nice icing on the cake. That would be amazing. So, I hope this is a direction that more smart glasses go. I hope this like ambient memory thing catches on more, too. I think these glasses are doing a lot of things right. If you'

[17:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'don\'t need speakers or a camera and you want really light, really stylish, really easy to control smart glasses that just feel really nice to wear and they\'re just really good and useful at what they do. These radio IOs might be for you if you can afford that $4.49 49'

[17:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to4.99 price point. You definitely don\'t need the charging case because it has 2 days of battery life, but it\'s translucent. I like it. It\'s cool. And it\'ll last more like a week plus if you have the charging case cuz you\'re going'

[17:58] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to put it in there at night. It\'s not going to die during the day and it\'s going to be fully charged by the next day. So, basically, until this case dies, your glasses aren\'t going to die. It\'s really cool. Unless you wear your glasses in your sleep, which I know you don\'t. And then lastly, these do support prescriptions, but they haven\'t'

[18:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'published like the official diopter range yet. And I\'m pretty sure if you get prescriptions then you won\'t be able to return them. But they do support them. So if that\'s something you\'re looking for, these could be really good for that, too. But let me know, what do you guys think about the Reineo IO smart glasses? Do you love them? Do you hate'

[18:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'them? Do you want a pair? Put all your thoughts down in the comments, as well as any video ideas you might have for this channel. Thank you so much for watching. You guys are the best. Until next time.'
